  "label": "Business analysis",
  "scope": "Analysing what a business needs and specifying what gets built or changed: eliciting and documenting requirements from stakeholders, mapping current and future processes, writing functional specifications, user journeys, use cases and user stories, and validating that the delivered solution meets the requirement (UAT support, walkthroughs). The subject can be software, data, platforms or operational process; the employer's industry is irrelevant. Covers every seniority from junior analyst to lead, and the hybrid titles this work hides under (requirements analyst, process analyst, digital/functional/technical business analyst). The edge: deciding WHAT the business needs is inside; owning the delivery schedule (IT project delivery) and owning the product vision (product management) are their own occupations beside it.",
